WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:09.230
In this walkthrough, we'll install release 3.8.22 using the Government State and Local content pack in GCC Moderate.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:13.351
We'll follow the same eight phases as the higher education guide.

00:00:14.151 --> 00:00:23.472
The footage comes from an internal lab installation, so the tenant, agency, and account names you see on screen are lab values, not values to copy.

00:00:24.272 --> 00:00:29.978
We'll verify the package, configure the settings, install the site, and review the result.

00:00:29.978 --> 00:00:36.255
Passing the automated checks is only part of deciding whether a deployment is ready for production.

00:00:37.082 --> 00:00:47.475
Download the release 3.8.22 implementation ZIP and its SHA256 receipt, not GitHub's automatically generated source archive.

00:00:48.275 --> 00:00:54.014
Run Get-FileHash on the ZIP and compare the result with the expected hash in the receipt.

00:00:54.014 --> 00:00:55.799
Continue only if they match.

00:00:56.599 --> 00:00:58.576
Use a new empty install folder.

00:00:58.576 --> 00:01:03.868
Copy the Government State and Local content pack to a separate organization folder.

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:09.862
Keep settings and records outside the extracted kit so a future release cannot overwrite them.

00:01:12.053 --> 00:01:18.317
Open Deployment-Settings.json in the organization folder, not the template inside the kit.

00:01:18.317 --> 00:01:25.047
Use the guide's comparison table to separate public agency information from tenant-specific settings.

00:01:25.847 --> 00:01:32.444
Confirm the tenant, SharePoint hosts, unused group alias, and approved owner and reviewer accounts.

00:01:33.244 --> 00:01:36.709
Keep the Team private and external sharing disabled.

00:01:36.709 --> 00:01:39.574
Set the LearningEnvironment to Government.

00:01:40.374 --> 00:01:45.438
If you're creating a new provisioning app, leave the PnP client ID blank.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:50.569
Don't copy another tenant's client ID or deployment report into this folder.

00:01:51.469 --> 00:01:53.893
Compare each setting with its source.

00:01:53.893 --> 00:02:04.049
Public policy links can be researched, but private mailboxes, ticket queues, incident routes, and tenant identities must come from the people who own them.

00:02:04.849 --> 00:02:07.339
Configure a monitored support mailbox.

00:02:07.339 --> 00:02:13.760
Then set the links for general support, technology requests, incident reporting, and AI guidance.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.771
Review the governance and training links as well.

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:26.499
Keep lasting changes to generated page text in the organization's Content folder, and approved reference files in Assets.

00:02:27.299 --> 00:02:32.344
The government governance drafts are examples for review, not adopted policy.

00:02:33.175 --> 00:02:39.522
From the extracted kit folder, run the local content preflight against the organization folder.

00:02:39.522 --> 00:02:41.726
The commands are shown on screen.

00:02:42.526 --> 00:02:49.341
This checks the structured content before sign-in, including the calendar columns and required fields.

00:02:49.341 --> 00:02:55.019
It does not approve the links, tenant settings, policy wording, or reader experience.

00:02:55.819 --> 00:02:58.692
Fix every reported issue before continuing.

00:02:59.526 --> 00:03:05.549
Use PowerShell 7.4 or later with PnP PowerShell 3.2.0.

00:03:06.349 --> 00:03:13.978
If the tenant needs a new provisioning app, have an administrator authorized to grant consent run script 01.

00:03:14.778 --> 00:03:19.730
The script saves the client ID before checking the public client setting.

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:25.419
If it stops at that check, correct the existing app rather than creating another one.

00:03:26.219 --> 00:03:34.182
In Entra, confirm that all required delegated permissions are granted and that Allow public client flows is set to Yes.

00:03:34.982 --> 00:03:37.057
Review the group naming policy.

00:03:37.057 --> 00:03:44.218
If it would change the alias, follow the organization's approved process for using an exempt administrator.

00:03:45.018 --> 00:03:56.261
Finally, check in the Teams admin center that the apps needed for the Website, PDF, PowerPoint, and SharePoint tabs are available to the installer and intended users.

00:03:56.261 --> 00:04:02.953
On each app's Users and groups tab, Availability should not say No one, as it does for Website here.

00:04:02.953 --> 00:04:09.512
Choose Edit availability, then make the app available to Everyone, or to specific users or groups.

00:04:09.512 --> 00:04:13.326
SharePoint, shown here, is already available to everyone.

00:04:15.661 --> 00:04:19.659
Run script 02 in Customer mode with SeedDemoContent.

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:26.124
Despite its name, that switch loads the site's pages, catalogs, calendar, and governance content.

00:04:26.924 --> 00:04:32.522
Customer mode controls the kit's generated demo notices and sample content behavior.

00:04:32.522 --> 00:04:37.187
It does not replace a review of the source files or published content.

00:04:37.987 --> 00:04:44.451
Before creating resources, check the signed-in account, tenant, alias, owner, and target address.

00:04:45.251 --> 00:04:52.316
If the installer flags a naming policy issue, an unconfigured route, or a lab mailbox, stop and review it.

00:04:52.316 --> 00:04:57.181
Choosing Proceed is a documented pilot decision, not production approval.

00:04:57.181 --> 00:05:03.045
The Admin Quickstart describes the same decision for a missing incident-reporting route.

00:05:03.845 --> 00:05:09.310
After installation, use the actual site address recorded in the deployment report.

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:11.976
Don't assume the path starts with sites.

00:05:11.976 --> 00:05:13.575
It may start with teams.

00:05:14.375 --> 00:05:20.573
If an earlier attempt already created resources for the alias, follow the recovery procedure.

00:05:20.573 --> 00:05:23.905
Don't start another clean installation against it.

00:05:26.372 --> 00:05:33.404
Run the read-only checker with the organization folder, the actual site address, and the same ContentMode.

00:05:33.404 --> 00:05:34.850
Resolve every failure.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:39.911
Read each warning and complete the review or corrective action it identifies.

00:05:40.711 --> 00:05:45.903
Review Home, the tool pages, navigation, and catalog views as a regular reader.

00:05:45.903 --> 00:05:48.532
Follow the support and governance links.

00:05:49.332 --> 00:05:58.994
Confirm the Team is private, external sharing is disabled, no demo content remains, and each standard channel has exactly one correct welcome post.

00:05:59.794 --> 00:06:04.197
The app does not normally have permission to read those posts back.

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:09.455
Check them visually rather than granting extra access just to clear the warning.

00:06:10.255 --> 00:06:13.738
Keep the checker output and the manual review record.

00:06:14.701 --> 00:06:22.084
Publish reviewed changes from the organization folder with script 03, Scope All, and interactive sign-in.

00:06:22.084 --> 00:06:26.919
Then run the same read-only checker and repeat the relevant manual review.

00:06:27.719 --> 00:06:31.247
Do not add RepairCapturedPages for a routine update.

00:06:31.247 --> 00:06:35.167
It can replace managed parts of Home and the captured pages.

00:06:35.167 --> 00:06:40.852
Use it only for a reviewed recovery, or an internal test where replacement is intended.

00:06:41.652 --> 00:06:50.668
Complete the handoff only when both checker runs have passed and the required manual reviews and approvals are documented for this tenant.

00:06:51.564 --> 00:06:55.521
Passing the checker is not the same as production approval.

00:06:55.521 --> 00:07:02.564
The organization still needs to approve the content, security, accessibility, and operating arrangements.

00:07:03.364 --> 00:07:11.346
Keep the organization settings, deployment reports, run logs, both checker outputs, and manual review records together.

00:07:12.146 --> 00:07:19.524
For recovery or removal, use the administrator guide included with release 3.8.22.

